      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/c4cdca/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-08-27T03:40:52.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It's interesting you brought up Bunker. An ability that says you can take a card into hand is probably a legit way to gain cards while in turret mode. Draw is a pretty core term, so I could see them being different since they didnt use that word.&nbsp;But mechanically speaking, taking the top card of your deck into hand is really the same thing as drawing a card. And in that case, should there even be a difference?although, in a situation where you reveal the top card and decide whether to put it into your hand or replace it then take it, I think I would be hesitant to call that drawing as those were both very different effects mechanically.With all that said, I think the safe answer Is to assume they are different (else why not just say draw for consistency sake).&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Unless I misread it, his text was take into hand from trash, not top of the deck. &nbsp;I think draw was another one of his abilities. &nbsp;It let me take Wrathful Retribution into hand and hit Omnitron for 29 to kill him. &nbsp;Interpolation Beam was out, so if I had to take the 1 damage from it, I would have lost instead.</p>",
